#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""lemlist — unofficial CLI over the lemlist REST API.

Not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by lemlist S.A.S.

Auto-generated from the OpenAPI spec sitting next to this script (openapi.json).
Covers every operation in the spec: GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE.

Set LEMLIST_API_KEY in your environment. JSON is written to stdout.

Quick start:
  export LEMLIST_API_KEY=...
  ./lemlist commands                   # list every available command
  ./lemlist help get-many-campaigns    # show args/flags for one command
  ./lemlist get-team
  ./lemlist get-many-campaigns --status running --all
  ./lemlist get-campaign cam_xxx
  ./lemlist create-campaign --name "My new campaign" --timezone Australia/Sydney
  ./lemlist update-campaign cam_xxx --body '{"name":"renamed"}'
  ./lemlist delete-schedule sch_xxx --dry-run    # preview without sending
  ./lemlist get-team --verbose                   # log the request line to stderr
  ./lemlist dump-all ../lemlist-data   # GET-only bulk snapshot
  ./lemlist dump-all ../lemlist-data --with-campaigns  # also drill per-campaign

Write methods (POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE) MUTATE your lemlist tenant.
`dump-all` only hits GET endpoints — it is always read-only.
Use --dry-run on write methods to preview the request without sending.

Other top-level flags:
  --version, -V    show CLI version
  --help, -h       show this help

Auth: lemlist uses HTTP Basic with the API key as the password and an
empty username. Override with --user if needed.
"""
